; X0 = ucontext -> W0 = 1 when the fault interrupted code running on this thread's alternate signal
; stack. Only the signal handler, and the runtime code it calls or leaves the thread in, runs there, so
; that is a fault inside the handler. The test keeps no state: a per-thread in-handler flag would stay
; set after the handler leaves by siglongjmp (guarded FFI recovery, an actor failing) and would need
; TLS, whose first use can allocate. sigaltstack(NULL, &ss) is a plain system call. A thread without an
; alternate stack (SS_DISABLE) answers 0; every thread the runtime creates has one. The bounds are strict at both
; ends: an actor's execution stack can be mapped directly below the alternate stack, so its top is
; the alternate stack's base, and the growth fault of the first push of a behavior interrupts code
; whose SP is exactly that base (a whole trial of idle actors reported a fault instead of running).
